60 edge (step_11). Static 3-hop paths do exist, e.g. 1006\u219245\u2192153\u21921860 (steps 03, 07, 10, 08) and 1006\u21921680\u21921390\u21921860 (steps 12, 14, 15).\n\nConfounder check: every candidate relay is a high-degree hub \u2014 45 (141 events / 126 partners), 153 (334 events / 253 partners, 5th most active node overall; steps 06, 09), and 1680 (74 out-neighbours). These nodes sit in ~1400 static triangles (step_13), so a static path from any low-degree node to any other is nearly guaranteed by hub popularity alone and carries no cascade evidence.\n\nCritical gap: every relation between 1006 and 1860 rests on **single, non-repeated** events (repeat_ratio 0.0342 graph-wide, step_01; each relevant edge has exactly 1 event, steps 07/08/10/14/15). None of the available tools expose event timestamps or allow restriction to [18031, 56431], so I cannot verify that the hops occur in increasing time order, that they fall inside the query window, or that consecutive hops are separated by \u2264600 time units. Given a horizon of 100000 and single-shot edges, the prior that three independent hub-mediated events happen to align within three 600-unit gaps is low, but I have no direct measurement either way.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_636b848d\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 45, 153, 1680, 1390],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No direct 1006->1860 edge exists. Static 3-hop routes exist (1006->45->153->1860 and 1006->1680->1390->1860), but every intermediary is a high-degree hub (153: 334 events/253 partners; 45: 126 partners; 1680: 74 out-neighbours) sitting in >1800 triangles, so time-ignoring reachability is explained by hub popularity rather than by a cascade. Each relevant edge fired exactly once, and the available tools report only whole-horizon aggregates with no timestamps and no windowing, so the ordering and the <=600-unit inter-hop delay inside [18031, 56431] cannot be verified. Evidence is therefore insufficient to affirm or deny a genuine time-respecting cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 35858, "total_output_tokens": 5620, "total_tokens": 41478, "total_latency_ms": 83271, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}